.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "Browserslist"
.PP

.PP
The config to share target browsers and Node\&.js versions between different front-end tools\&. It is used in:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRAutoprefixer\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRBabel\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRpostcss-preset-env\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fReslint-plugin-compat\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRstylelint-no-unsupported-browser-features\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRpostcss-normalize\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRobsolete-webpack-plugin\fP
.PP

.PP
All tools will find target browsers automatically, when you add the following to \fRpackage\&.json\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
"browserslist": [
  "defaults and fully supports es6\-module",
  "maintained node versions"
]
.fi
.PP

.PP
Or in \fR\&.browserslistrc\fP config:

.PP
.PP
.nf
# Browsers that we support

defaults and fully supports es6\-module
maintained node versions
.fi
.PP

.PP
Developers set their version lists using queries like \fRlast 2 versions\fP to be free from updating versions manually\&. Browserslist will use \fR\fRcaniuse-lite\fP\fP with \fRCan I Use\fP data for this queries\&.

.PP
You can check how config works at our playground: \fR\fRbrowsersl\&.ist\fP\fP

.PP
\fR \fP

.PP

